  "raw": {
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4417735": {
      "title": "Thomas College - Admissions In-House Counselor and Visit Coordinator",
      "description": "Thomas College - Admissions In-House Counselor and Visit Coordinator In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Admissions In-House Counselor and Visit Coordinator Thomas College Apply Admissions In-House Counselor and Visit Coordinator Waterville, ME • Admissions Apply Job Type Full-time Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine’s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program™, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn’t a buzzword; it’s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. As a member of the admissions team, the Admissions In-house Counselor and Visit Coordinator provides admission counseling and enrollment services support. The position oversees the scheduling and execution of group visits, and conducts individual student interviews/meetings, through which s/he serves as a permanent, in-house point of contact for visiting prospective students and families, and guides students through the admissions process. This role participates in the annual review of applications for admission and the awarding of scholarships. The role also provides shared administrative support for Admissions, Student Financial Services, and the Registrar by answering routine questions, triaging calls and messages, and ensuring inquiries reach the appropriate person for timely follow-up. This role is designed to strengthen the visitor experience, provide an enhanced level of admission counseling, and maintain responsive campus coverage throughout the admissions cycle. Limited recruitment travel, evening work, and weekend responsibilities may be required during peak periods. The qualified candidate will coordinate and deliver individual and group campus visits, including scheduling, personalized itineraries, faculty and staff appointments, student ambassador coverage, visitor communications, welcoming guests, and post-visit follow up. Will serve as an in-house admission counselor by guiding prospective students and families through the admissions process, responding to questions, conducting presentations and interviews, supporting application completion, and completing assigned outreach and conversion activities. Bachelor’s Degree is required. Must have experience in customer service, experience in admissions, enrollemnt services, higher education, student services, or a related field preferred. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and presentation skills. Ability to think critically and exercise judgment in the review of student applications for admission and scholarship. Enthusiastic, positive, student-centered mindset with the ability to create a welcoming experience for students and families. Ability to manage multiple priorities, maintain detailed records, exercise sound judgment, and coordinate work across several offices. Ability to explain routine College processes clearly and recognize when a question must be referred to other College offices. Proficiency with Microsoft Suite. Experience with, or ability to learn, Slate CRM and other College systems used by Admissions, Student Financial Services, and the Registrar. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities. Salary Description $26.60 - $27.00 an hour Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
