    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4394800": {
      "title": "Thomas College",
      "description": "Thomas College - Student Financial Services Counselor In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Student Financial Services Counselor Thomas College Apply Student Financial Services Counselor Waterville, ME • Student Financial Services Apply Job Type Full-time Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine’s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program™, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn’t a buzzword; it’s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. The SFS Counselor is accountable for ensuring that all aspects of student billing and accounts are processed accurately, efficiently, and in compliance with institutional policies and federal regulations. This role has extensive contact with students, families, and campus partners and plays a critical part in supporting student success through timely and transparent account management. The qualified candidate works daily with students and families to resolve outstanding balances and establish payment plans. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of options and resources available to help students meet their financial obligations. Prepares and maintains accurate student bills, including monthly billing cycles. Collaborates with the Controller’s office to ensure accurate reconciliation and reporting. Monitors outstanding balances and communicate regularly with students no longer enrolled. Ensures timely documentation and collection of funds from external partners. Associate’s degree required; Bachelor’s degree preferred. Two or more years of experience in student accounts, bursar operations, billing, collections, or related financial operations strongly preferred. Strong technical skills with student information systems, financial databases, and Microsoft Office Suite. Excellent communication skills with the ability to provide clear, empathetic, and professional service to students and families. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities. Salary Description $48,000 to $54,000 Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4394597": {
      "title": "Thomas College",
      "description": "Thomas College - Student Financial Services Financial Aid Counselor In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Student Financial Services Financial Aid Counselor Thomas College Apply Student Financial Services Financial Aid Counselor Waterville, ME • Student Financial Services Apply Job Type Full-time Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine’s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program™, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn’t a buzzword; it’s a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. For more information visit Thomas.edu. The Student Financial Services Financial Aid Counselor (SFS FAC) is accountable for performing all necessary support functions of the Financial Aid processed in a timely and accurate manner. The SFS FAC assists with processing ISIR’s and collects all data required of a financial aid applicant and sends correspondence to the student to encourage prompt submission of missing information and verification procedures. The SFS FAC also helps maintain entrance counseling compliance, master promissory notes and annual student loan acknowledgement is completed before funds are disbursed to student’s accounts. Including review of accurate sub-loan levels for students each term and making adjustments as necessary. When prospective students and their parents come to campus for a tour, the SFS FAC may meet with the families to discuss the financial aid procedures and processes. These meetings are done in person, virtual meetings, telephone and email communications. The SFS FAC completes all tasks associated with acceptance, rejection, corrections, and updates to awards. The SFS FAC provides a second review of all financial aid awards to ensure federal and state compliance. The SFS FAC must also update the in-process data that reflects aid pending on the student's tuition account. When funds arrive at the college from alternative loans and scholarships. The SFS FAC is also responsible for helping students and families file the FAFSA annually. The SFS FAC position requires a person who is articulate and friendly, with a professional appearance. Computer experience is critical. The person must be able to maintain an orderly workspace and be able to withstand frequent interruptions. He/She must be able to relate well to people over the age of fifteen. This job involves a combination of customer service skills and technical office skills. Willingness to provide students with support with a variety of campus issues and knowledgeable with other department functions, to direct students where they need to go. An Associate Degree is required, Bachelor’s Degree is preferred. Two to three years of financial aid experience is required. Strong written and verbal communication skills are a must. The ideal candidate needs to be a team player and willing to work hard to support our students and the institution. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities. Salary Description $48,000 to $54,000 Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4371025": {
      "title": "Thomas College - Associate Director of Disability Services and Student Support",
      "description": "Thomas College - Associate Director of Disability Services and Student Support In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Associate Director of Disability Services and Student Support Thomas College Apply Associate Director of Disability Services and Student Support Waterville, ME • Student Affairs Apply Job Type Full-time Description U.S. News and World Report consistently ranks Thomas College as a top college in Maine for social mobility. Our clear career focus and one-of-a-kind Guaranteed Job Program™ makes it possible to advance faster in the arts and sciences, business, and education. Earn an undergraduate degree in three years and then choose from a variety of in-person or online graduate degree programs that can be completed in one-year or two. Located in Waterville, Maine, Thomas College is your pathway to a promising future, guaranteed. Learn more at thomas.edu . The Associate Director of Disability Services and Student Support will be responsible for coordinating support services for students with disabilities at Thomas College. This role will ensure compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act while fostering an inclusive and accessible learning environment. The Associate Director will be a member of the Student Affairs team, reporting to the Vice President of Student Affairs, and will work collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff to provide accommodations and promote awareness of disability-related issues. Occasional evening and weekend work required. The qualified candidate will evaluate, process, and implement reasonable accommodations for students with disabilities; provide direct support and advising to students regarding academic accommodations, assistive technology, and self-advocacy. The qualified candidate will also develop educational materials and deliver workshops and training sessions for students, faculty, and staff on disability awareness and accessibility. Must have a Bachelor’s degree in education, counseling, social work or a related field (Master’s preferred). Must have a minimum of two years of experience in disability services or related field. Must have a strong knowledge of disability laws, including ADA and Section 504. Thomas offers a competitive benefits package to include: Medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, 6% 403(b) matching plan, paid vacation, paid sick leave, thirteen paid holidays, on-site gym, meal discounts and free tuition for employees, spouse and dependent children. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities. Salary Description $65,000 to $70,000 Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
