ement, and program logistics Maintain a high standard of professionalism, accountability, and commitment to student-athlete well-being Ensure full compliance with NCAA Division III, National Collegiate Rugby (NCR) and North Atlantic Collegiate Rugby (NACR), and Thomas College policies and procedures The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong communication skills, organizational ability, a passion for player development, and a commitment to fostering a positive and competitive team culture. Bachelor’s degree is required. Must have a valid driver’s license and ability to travel regionally. Must have the ability to work evenings/weekends, and travel with the team as needed. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities. Salary Description $1,000 - $1,500 annual stipend Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
