      "title": "Thomas College - Part-Time Assistant Men’s Baseball Coach",
      "description": "Thomas College - Part-Time Assistant Men’s Baseball Coach In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Part-Time Assistant Men’s Baseball Coach Thomas College Apply Part-Time Assistant Men’s Baseball Coach Waterville, ME • Athletics Apply Job Type Part-time Description Thomas College, located in beautiful Waterville, Maine, is defining what it means to be the College of the Future. With a strong commitment to innovation, career readiness, and community partnerships, Thomas College is consistently ranked by U.S. News & World Report as one of Maine’s top colleges for social mobility. Our distinctive Guaranteed Job Program™, accelerated undergraduate degrees, and flexible graduate programs empower students to advance faster in business, entrepreneurship, education, technology, applied STEM, and arts & science fields. At Thomas, belonging isn't a buzzword; it's a promise. We create a supportive, welcoming environment where every student is seen, valued, and prepared to thrive in a rapidly changing world. Thomas College is an NCAA Division III school and a member of the North Atlantic Conference (NAC). Learn more at athletics.thomas.edu . Thomas College Baseball is seeking qualified applicants for a part-time Assistant Coach. The successful candidate will assist in all aspects of the program, including both competitive success and student-athlete development. Primary Responsibilities: Assist in building and sustaining a strong and organized recruiting pipeline aligned with program needs Assist in planning and conducting practices, training sessions, and individual player development consistent with the Head Coach’s vision Contribute to match preparation, including scouting, video analysis, and game-day coaching Support team operations, including travel coordination, equipment management, and program logistics Maintain a high standard of professionalism, accountability, and commitment to student-athlete well-being Ensure full compliance with NCAA Division III, North Atlantic Conference (NAC), and Thomas College policies and procedures The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong communication skills, organizational ability, a passion for player development, and a commitment to fostering a positive and competitive team culture. Bachelor’s degree is required. Must have a valid driver’s license and ability to travel regionally. Must have the ability to work evenings/weekends, and travel with the team as needed. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume and names of three professional references. Please include an email address on your application materials. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Thomas College is an equal opportunity employer. Thomas College's mission is to prepare students for success in their personal and professional lives, and for leadership and service in their communities. Salary Description $4,500 annual stipend Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
